1
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,740
There's always a door.

2
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:11,756
I've spent my whole life watching the light under one.

3
00:00:11,956 --> 00:00:15,779
The last time, I was face down on a massage table,

4
00:00:15,779 --> 00:00:17,308
counting my breaths.

5
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:21,283
And all I could think was: if I move one muscle, one

6
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:25,335
of us is going to jail, and one of us is leaving here

7
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:26,782
on a stretcher.

8
00:00:26,982 --> 00:00:28,443
So I didn't move.

9
00:00:28,643 --> 00:00:30,669
People ask me why I froze.

10
00:00:30,869 --> 00:00:32,805
Because it wasn't the first time.

11
00:00:36,005 --> 00:00:37,546
I was two the first time.

12
00:00:37,546 --> 00:00:38,833
Twelve the last.

13
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:40,899
Someone in my own family.

14
00:00:40,899 --> 00:00:43,287
A child, not much older than me.

15
00:00:43,287 --> 00:00:46,271
They said my favorite cousin did it too.

16
00:00:46,271 --> 00:00:47,989
That it was normal.

17
00:00:48,189 --> 00:00:51,194
At twelve, I said the bravest word I knew.

18
00:00:51,194 --> 00:00:51,708
No.

19
00:00:51,908 --> 00:00:53,757
And that door stayed shut.

20
00:00:53,957 --> 00:00:57,822
Years later I found out the ones who opened it had

21
00:00:57,822 --> 00:01:00,605
been hurt behind doors of their own.

22
00:01:00,605 --> 00:01:02,306
That's how it travels.

23
00:01:02,306 --> 00:01:03,465
Child to child.

24
00:01:03,465 --> 00:01:04,770
Door to door.

25
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:06,660
My first job.

26
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,649
A shoe store.

27
00:01:07,649 --> 00:01:11,607
My boss asked me to help him bring boxes up from the

28
00:01:11,607 --> 00:01:12,592
basement.

29
00:01:12,792 --> 00:01:15,806
At the bottom of those stairs, he kissed me.

30
00:01:16,006 --> 00:01:17,040
I didn't move.

31
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:20,362
I waited until his footsteps reached the top.

32
00:01:20,362 --> 00:01:24,576
Then I walked out the front door and never came back.

33
00:01:24,776 --> 00:01:27,928
I begged my boyfriend, don't tell my daddy.

34
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:29,247
He told him first.

35
00:01:29,247 --> 00:01:32,333
The two of them tore that store apart.

36
00:01:32,533 --> 00:01:33,894
And I reported him.

37
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:37,238
At the mall, a man brought me a gift.

38
00:01:37,238 --> 00:01:38,753
Every single day.

39
00:01:38,953 --> 00:01:40,170
I switched stores.

40
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,891
He found the new one.

41
00:01:42,091 --> 00:01:46,185
When a coworker stood beside me, he'd step outside and

42
00:01:46,185 --> 00:01:47,929
wait by the glass door.

43
00:01:47,929 --> 00:01:48,612
Watching.

44
00:01:48,612 --> 00:01:49,670
For weeks.

45
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:51,331
I called the police.

46
00:01:52,031 --> 00:01:55,931
I learned to work in rooms where men tip you to smile.

47
00:01:55,931 --> 00:01:58,109
I learned to laugh it off.

48
00:01:58,309 --> 00:02:01,868
Then a contractor at my parents' house hugged me

49
00:02:01,868 --> 00:02:05,649
goodbye at the front door, and his hands went where

50
00:02:05,649 --> 00:02:07,951
they had no business going.

51
00:02:08,151 --> 00:02:12,105
I told my mother, only because my little sisters lived

52
00:02:12,105 --> 00:02:12,544
there.

53
00:02:12,544 --> 00:02:13,577
She asked:

54
00:02:14,027 --> 00:02:15,400
MOM: What did you have on?

55
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:17,526
Then she caught herself.

56
00:02:17,526 --> 00:02:21,110
But some questions don't go back in your mouth.

57
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:22,315
A date.

58
00:02:22,315 --> 00:02:26,224
A room with nothing in it but a bed, wall to wall.

59
00:02:26,424 --> 00:02:28,574
I fought my way to that door.

60
00:02:28,574 --> 00:02:29,315
I got out.

61
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:31,616
He kept every dollar I had.

62
00:02:31,816 --> 00:02:33,592
That one I never reported.

63
00:02:33,592 --> 00:02:35,943
I told myself I'd been stupid.

64
00:02:36,843 --> 00:02:38,305
Look at what I did.

65
00:02:38,305 --> 00:02:40,382
At twelve, I used my voice.

66
00:02:40,382 --> 00:02:43,614
In that basement, I waited, then I walked.

67
00:02:43,614 --> 00:02:45,684
On that date, I fought.

68
00:02:45,884 --> 00:02:48,123
Every time, I found a way out.

69
00:02:48,323 --> 00:02:49,673
Until the table.

70
00:02:50,873 --> 00:02:55,015
Years later, I was a mother carrying everything in my

71
00:02:55,015 --> 00:02:55,406
back.

72
00:02:55,406 --> 00:02:58,141
So I did what everybody says to do.

73
00:02:58,141 --> 00:02:59,926
I booked a massage.

74
00:03:00,126 --> 00:03:01,336
He was licensed.

75
00:03:01,336 --> 00:03:03,830
His certificate hung by the door.

76
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:06,246
He knew my children's names.

77
00:03:06,446 --> 00:03:10,040
I lay face down and let my guard down for the first

78
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:11,396
time in months.

79
00:03:11,596 --> 00:03:15,281
Then his hands went where a therapist's hands have no

80
00:03:15,281 --> 00:03:16,484
reason to go.

81
00:03:16,684 --> 00:03:19,686
The first time, I told myself I was wrong.

82
00:03:19,686 --> 00:03:23,632
The second time, there was nothing left to believe.

83
00:03:25,332 --> 00:03:26,739
And I didn't move.

84
00:03:26,939 --> 00:03:30,431
I've stood up to principals, landlords, police

85
00:03:30,431 --> 00:03:31,949
officers and judges.

86
00:03:31,949 --> 00:03:35,137
But on that table, my mouth wouldn't open.

87
00:03:35,137 --> 00:03:39,236
If I move, one of us goes to jail and one of us leaves

88
00:03:39,236 --> 00:03:40,375
on a stretcher.

89
00:03:40,375 --> 00:03:42,577
I didn't know if I could win.

90
00:03:42,577 --> 00:03:45,913
And if I lost, next time could be worse.

91
00:03:46,113 --> 00:03:48,834
So I watched the light under the door.

92
00:03:48,834 --> 00:03:50,064
And I waited.

93
00:03:50,264 --> 00:03:53,437
When it was over, he said, "Take your time getting

94
00:03:53,437 --> 00:03:53,990
up."

95
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:54,631
I paid.

96
00:03:54,631 --> 00:03:55,750
I tipped him.

97
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:59,338
Then I sat in my car for forty minutes with one

98
00:03:59,338 --> 00:03:59,987
question:

99
00:03:59,987 --> 00:04:02,233
Why didn't you do anything?

100
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:06,462
Weeks later, I told my boyfriend, Andre.

101
00:04:06,462 --> 00:04:07,446
He was quiet.

102
00:04:07,446 --> 00:04:10,472
Then he asked, not mean, just tired:

103
00:04:10,922 --> 00:04:12,114
ANDRE: What did you have on?

104
00:04:12,564 --> 00:04:13,859
The same question.

105
00:04:13,859 --> 00:04:14,723
Years later.

106
00:04:14,723 --> 00:04:16,317
A different mouth.

107
00:04:16,517 --> 00:04:17,965
Then I told my dad.

108
00:04:18,415 --> 00:04:20,265
DAD: Let it go, baby girl.

109
00:04:20,265 --> 00:04:22,114
DAD: You know how you get.

110
00:04:22,114 --> 00:04:25,233
DAD: Don't make it bigger than it is.

111
00:04:25,683 --> 00:04:27,509
So I closed the door again.

112
00:04:27,509 --> 00:04:29,364
And I stayed behind it.

113
00:04:30,564 --> 00:04:33,841
One night I read about the freeze response.

114
00:04:33,841 --> 00:04:36,355
Most people know fight or flight.

115
00:04:36,355 --> 00:04:37,879
There's a third one.

116
00:04:37,879 --> 00:04:41,918
When your body decides that fighting or running could

117
00:04:41,918 --> 00:04:44,585
get you hurt worse, it holds still.

118
00:04:44,585 --> 00:04:45,804
The voice locks.

119
00:04:45,804 --> 00:04:47,404
The muscles go heavy.

120
00:04:47,404 --> 00:04:48,852
It isn't agreement.

121
00:04:48,852 --> 00:04:50,224
It isn't weakness.

122
00:04:50,224 --> 00:04:53,191
It's survival, faster than thought.

123
00:04:53,391 --> 00:04:56,005
I sat on my kitchen floor and cried.

124
00:04:56,005 --> 00:04:57,820
Not because I was broken.

125
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:01,098
Because I finally understood I never was.

126
00:05:01,298 --> 00:05:05,010
The next morning I called the state licensing board

127
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:06,612
and filed a complaint.

128
00:05:06,612 --> 00:05:08,586
I made a police report.

129
00:05:08,786 --> 00:05:10,418
People said, "Why now?

130
00:05:10,418 --> 00:05:13,979
You're doing too much." I wasn't doing too much.

131
00:05:13,979 --> 00:05:17,692
I had carried it alone until it got too heavy.

132
00:05:17,892 --> 00:05:19,047
Andre came around.

133
00:05:19,047 --> 00:05:21,079
He sat next to me and said,

134
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:23,375
ANDRE: I asked you the wrong question.

135
00:05:23,375 --> 00:05:24,270
ANDRE: I'm sorry.

136
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:27,281
My dad still doesn't fully get it.

137
00:05:27,281 --> 00:05:29,617
But he drove me to the hearing.

138
00:05:29,617 --> 00:05:32,178
Sometimes love doesn't understand.

139
00:05:32,178 --> 00:05:34,512
Sometimes it just shows up.

140
00:05:35,412 --> 00:05:40,116
The Bible says, "The Lord is nigh unto them that are

141
00:05:40,116 --> 00:05:43,011
of a broken heart." Psalm 34:18.

142
00:05:43,011 --> 00:05:47,444
And, "There is nothing covered, that shall not be

143
00:05:47,444 --> 00:05:49,644
revealed." Luke 12:2.

144
00:05:49,844 --> 00:05:52,384
If you froze, you did not consent.

145
00:05:52,384 --> 00:05:55,746
If you were a child, it was never your fault.

146
00:05:55,746 --> 00:05:59,407
If you waited years to speak, you were not lying.

147
00:05:59,407 --> 00:06:03,218
And what you wore never put anybody's hands on you.

148
00:06:03,218 --> 00:06:04,564
They did that.

149
00:06:04,764 --> 00:06:08,465
Have you ever been asked the wrong question after

150
00:06:08,465 --> 00:06:10,429
something happened to you?

151
00:06:10,429 --> 00:06:12,242
Tell me in the comments.

152
00:06:12,242 --> 00:06:16,094
Somebody reading needs to know they're not the only

153
00:06:16,094 --> 00:06:16,696
one.

154
00:06:17,396 --> 00:06:21,148
If this happened to you, you don't have to carry it

155
00:06:21,148 --> 00:06:21,589
alone.

156
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,943
Open the Community Covenant app.

157
00:06:23,943 --> 00:06:26,223
The link is in the description.

158
00:06:26,223 --> 00:06:29,975
If you're in the U.S. and want to talk to a lawyer,

159
00:06:29,975 --> 00:06:33,652
the free legal referral form is in the description

160
00:06:33,652 --> 00:06:33,947
too.

161
00:06:33,947 --> 00:06:37,998
We are not attorneys, and this is not legal advice.

162
00:06:38,198 --> 00:06:42,064
If you're in danger right now, call 911.

163
00:06:42,064 --> 00:06:46,993
In the U.S., the National Sexual Assault Hotline is

164
00:06:46,993 --> 00:06:52,019
1-800-656-4673, any time, day or night, and it helps

165
00:06:52,019 --> 00:06:55,596
adults who were hurt as children too.

166
00:06:55,596 --> 00:07:00,428
If you're thinking about hurting yourself, call or

167
00:07:00,428 --> 00:07:01,598
text 988.
